    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scillĭnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκίλλινος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of sea-onions</i>
			or <i>squills</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acetum,</span>”
				<i>vinegar flavored with squills</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 2, 28, § 59</span></i>
			; also called acetum scilliticum (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιλλιτικόν</span>), <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				19, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 32,
				10, 47, § 135</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm.
				510</span></i>.</div>
